34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The transport costs are far more volatile than the lodging. We must prioritize a location that minimizes travel expenses to keep the fee stable.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,We should avoid locations that require extensive manual labor or complex application processes. The administrative burden on the organizers is a critical factor.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,It seems our previous camps failed to integrate the members. We need a destination that forces us to spend time together in a shared space.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I have found that some inland options can be quite restrictive and crowded, which might lead to poor sleep and exhaustion.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The current flat-fee system is problematic. If we choose a whole-building let, the risk of last-minute cancellations falling on the remaining members is high.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, I agree. A fixed cost per person based on public rates is safer than a whole-building let that we have to subsidize.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"If we choose a public facility with a lottery system, the paperwork is immense. A private facility with a simple booking would be more sustainable.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, while costs matter, a cheap camp that half the members skip is a waste of resources. We need a cohesive environment.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"If the rooms are overcrowded, the quality of the training sessions will suffer. We should seek a place with adequate personal space.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"We need to be transparent about the ""side costs."" A destination with an all-inclusive canteen would prevent the uneven spending I suspect is happening.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minako, cohesion is a goal, but financial stability is a requirement. I cannot support a destination that risks another budget shortfall.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, you mentioned the canteen. A place with professional catering would eliminate the cooking duty, which is a significant drain on the organizers.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,I am not suggesting we overspend. I am suggesting we prioritize a layout that prevents the club from splitting into isolated year-groups.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I believe we should prioritize a location that guarantees a quiet environment. Rest is the foundation of any successful training camp.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we use a public bed facility, the rates are fixed and transparent. This minimizes the risk of hidden costs and unfair distributions.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Let us focus on the options that balance low transport costs with fixed, transparent lodging rates.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I will support any option that minimizes the administrative and physical labor required from the organizing committee.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I will vote for the option that best facilitates interaction between the different year-groups, regardless of the location's prestige.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will vote for the option that ensures the members can actually sleep and recover between the training sessions.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I will vote for the option that is most financially transparent and least susceptible to losses from last-minute cancellations.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
