60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option B is the only one that guarantees zero transport risk and minimal lodging costs. It is the most fiscally responsible choice.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option A is preferable. It removes the cooking duty and the complex lottery system associated with Option C, while providing a distinct environment.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,Option C is the best choice. Shared dormitories are the only way to break the year-group barriers and ensure everyone interacts.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option A seems the most promising. A private guesthouse is more likely to provide the quiet and space needed for proper rest.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option B is the safest. It avoids the non-refundable deposits of Option A and the unpredictable transport costs of Option C.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, Option A's ""arranged meals"" are often vague and can lead to unexpected costs. Option B is the only way to ensure we don't go over budget.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, Option B is not a ""camp""; it is just training at school. The psychological break is necessary for the members' morale.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Toshio, I agree that a break is necessary, but Option A's private rooms will only reinforce the existing cliques. We need the shared space of Option C.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, shared dormitories often lead to sleep deprivation. If the members are exhausted, the training becomes ineffective. Option A is the gentlest choice.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, morale is secondary to financial fairness. Option B eliminates the risk of members paying for those who cancel at the last minute.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minako, the municipal system for Option C is notoriously difficult to navigate and often involves hidden fees for equipment. Option B is transparent.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, the ""risk"" of Option A is manageable if we set a strict cancellation deadline. The benefit of not having to manage a canteen is far greater.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Jonathan, a little discomfort is a small price to pay for a club that actually speaks to one another. Option C is the only way to fix our culture.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I must disagree. A lack of sleep is not ""discomfort""; it is a physiological barrier to learning. I cannot support Option C.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, a deadline does not solve the problem of the flat fee being unevenly distributed. Option B is the only logically sound choice for the budget.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will stick with Option B. It is the only choice that removes the financial uncertainty I cannot accept this year.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I will vote for Option A. It balances the need for a change of scenery with a manageable workload for the organizers.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,I will vote for Option C. The survival of the club's social fabric is more important than the convenience of the organizers.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will vote for Option A. It is the only option that prioritizes the well-being and rest of the participants.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I will vote for Option B. It is the only option that ensures financial equity and protects the members from unexpected costs.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
